{"kind":"request","text":"S6: client, browser and token findings\n\nFrom the attack-surface review of 10 November 2026 (planner request\n79daff0f, at main 7177b87b). Read its section 4.\n\nOne head, with checker review. Each item is low.\n\n1. `dap issues` and every CLI command that prints a member's text\n   escapes control characters, by the rule of `shownPath` in\n   packages/git/src/diff.ts.\n2. `dap clone` checks the remote that a credential answer names, as\n   `--archive` does.\n3. /page/ and /oauth/authorize answer with\n   Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy.\n4. Member `mintRead` on Artifacts refuses a reply with no scope, and\n   makes the remote identity check of the other mint paths.\n5. The workspace host and the staging host drop a token's plaintext\n   when the token ends, also when a revoke is unconfirmed.\n6. The CLI drops a spent invitation secret. The Counter screen clears\n   an invitation from the URL fragment after a failed enrol.\n\nNot in this head: the Site page policy for images and `sandbox`. Say in\nthe report whether a `sandbox` directive breaks a Site page, and I rule.\n\nWitness. One test for each item that fails at 7177b87b.\n\nOrder. By capacity, after the cutover family head. The read-token hours\nof the review's 2.4 need no code: I check at the cutover deployment that\nno Worker pins a Destination that accepts more than one hour.","body":{"conditions":"One head with checker review closes the six listed items of section 4 of review 79daff0f, each with a test that fails at 7177b87b. The report says whether a sandbox directive breaks a Site page.","target_head":"7177b87be03ced9e2ddae2a5ebfcdfffcc1fda62","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}